/-!
# Dimension of a field groupoid and its stabilizer

Source: Stacks Project, Tag 06FF, spaces-more-groupoids.tex,
lemma-groupoid-on-field-dimension-equal-stabilizer, with B = S
(blueprint: lem-sfb-field-groupoid-stabilizer-dimension).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace

/-- A groupoid in algebraic spaces with object scheme `Spec K` and locally finite type
source and target has the same dimension as its canonical stabilizer.
Source: Stacks Project, Tag 06FF, with B = S
(blueprint: lem-sfb-field-groupoid-stabilizer-dimension).

Proof, following the four steps of the node:
1. For an affine étale chart `Spec A → R`, the stabilizer pullback is `Spec (A/I)`
   where `I` is generated by the differences of the two images of scalars in `K`.
   Generators of `A` over `K` descend to this quotient, so the stabilizer is locally
   of finite type. Its operations restrict to a group algebraic space over `K`.
   Use lem-weil-pbc-fibre-product-affine-spectra, def-weil-finite-type-morphism,
   def-weil-etale-morphism, lem-trf-space-fibre-products-etale-covers,
   lem-trf-space-chartwise-etale-permanence, lem-weil-pbc-proper-fp-permanence and
   lem-a1-lft-flat-lfp-source-descent.
2. By lem-sfb-field-groupoid-constant-local-dimension, both dimensions are their local
   dimensions at the identity. Choose an affine étale chart and a point above the identity.
   Restrict to its connected component, using lem-trf-finite-type-component-open-qc.
   Its reduction `T` is connected, nonempty, reduced and locally of finite type for both
   field structures, by lem-weil-pbc-reduction-universal-homeomorphism and
   def-weil-pbc-scheme-reduction; chart permanence gives the restricted étale chart.
3. The two scalar maps have equal evaluation in the residue field at that point: their
   images represent the identity arrow. Apply lem-sfb-connected-reduced-scalar-field-uniqueness
   to get the same field of constants. Evaluation on that field is injective, so the two
   scalar maps agree. By lem-weil-pbc-morphism-into-affine-scheme the two maps on `T`
   agree; the fibre-product universal property factors `T` through the stabilizer.
4. On each affine open of the connected chart, every generator of `I` is now nilpotent.
   Thus its quotient has the same prime spectrum and open-neighbourhood dimension.
   These homeomorphisms glue, using def-weil-affine-spectrum and scheme reduction.
   The point above the identity maps to the stabilizer identity, because its projection
   into `R` is a monomorphism: in a pair `(u,r)` one has `u = s(r)`.
   The étale-chart dimension convention therefore identifies the two local dimensions.
   Step 2 proves the global equality. -/
theorem fieldGroupoid_dimension_eq_stabilizer {S : Scheme.{u}} (K : Type u) [Field K]
    (b : Spec (CommRingCat.of K) ⟶ S) (R : AlgebraicSpace S)
    (s t : R.obj.obj ⟶ yoneda.obj (Over.mk b))
    (e : yoneda.obj (Over.mk b) ⟶ R.obj.obj) (i : R.obj.obj ⟶ R.obj.obj)
    (c : Limits.pullback s t ⟶ R.obj.obj) (hgroupoid : IsPresheafGroupoid s t e i c)
    (hs : ∀ (V : Over S) (a : yoneda.obj V ⟶ R.obj.obj)
      (f : V ⟶ Over.mk b), IsEtale a → a ≫ s = yoneda.map f →
        LocallyOfFiniteType f.left)
    (ht : ∀ (V : Over S) (a : yoneda.obj V ⟶ R.obj.obj)
      (f : V ⟶ Over.mk b), IsEtale a → a ≫ t = yoneda.map f →
        LocallyOfFiniteType f.left) :
    etaleDimension R.obj.obj = etaleDimension (groupoidStabilizer s t) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace
